(defmodule vc
  "**Version control** — git's and mur's porcelains over one shared core.

The context's details live under `src/vc/`: what every backend shares (`vc/vcscore`: the
backend registry C-x g and C-x v dispatch through, the mode line's branch; `vc/vcsproc`: the
process log and the queue no VCS command blocks a key in), git's porcelain (`vc/git` and the
`vc/git*` parts it loads) and mur's (`vc/mur` and the `vc/mur*` parts), the merge-conflict
mode (`vc/smerge`) and the time machine (`vc/timemachine`). A diff is painted by the `diffs`
context.

Other contexts reach version control through its commands — C-x g, C-x v, the keys a status
buffer binds — never through its details: loading this module loads both backends, so each
registers its row in the core and is offered."
  ;; loaded with the context: each backend registers its row in `vc/vcscore` at load, and a
  ;; backend whose row has not loaded is not offered
  (:use vc/gitbar :only []) ; git's row: C-x g, C-x v, the mode line's branch
  (:use vc/mur :only [])) ; mur's, with all of its porcelain
